# SDD bridge: code-knowledge-graph-engineering

## Selection

Use for: Node/edge schema, provenance, impact analysis, paths, clusters and subgraph/density visualization.

Do not select for: a marketing graph or static presentation; use design-system/design-review. Do not replace a compiler/LSP with embeddings.

## Inputs and contributions

Known inputs: stable identities, extracted/inferred relationships, snapshots, impact queries, cardinality and layout limits. Do not infer missing capabilities or permissions.

| Artifact | Required input / contribution |
|---|---|
| Constitution | Reconcile existing authorization, data residency, safety and project constraints; add no product policy automatically. |
| Spec | Define scoped, observable behavior and rejected cases. Nodes/edges have types, identity and provenance bound to the snapshot. |
| Plan / ADR | Compare alternatives, contract versions and failure modes; link REQ, AC, D and R IDs; preserve authority boundaries. Typed node/edge model with stable IDs and a per-snapshot source of truth. |
| Tasks | Name actual files, fixtures, tools, real permissions, failure injections and completion checks. Test incremental invalidation and distinguish inferences. |
| Evidence / convergence | Identify observed implementation/oracle/configuration versions and hashes, test results, unsatisfied criteria and explicit limits. versioned graph contract, bounded queries, edge traceability, invalidation policies, structural/dense modes |

## Conditional handoff

Optional specialist: `code-context-engineering`. Specific unresolved question: “Can the edge's origin be verified in the indexed code snapshot?” Consult only if actually present and needed. Supply relevant IDs, known facts, unknowns, permission scope, versions and required evidence. Do not install or load a whole dependency chain. Continue independent work and mark blocked criteria unverified.

## Completion and authority

Shared routing, authorization, outcome states and documentation closure follow
[workflow](../workflow.md) and [evidence](../evidence.md). This bridge maps a
selected method to artifacts; it neither activates skills nor changes permissions.
For reuse elsewhere, keep these shared contracts and adapt skill_path to that project.
